wg-easy + Caddy, deployed by Ansible (role wg_easy)

  Web UI        https://{{ wg_easy_domain }}
  Admin user    {{ wg_easy_admin_user }}
  Admin pass    {{ wg_easy_admin_password_final }}

  VPN endpoint  {{ wg_easy_host_final }}:{{ wg_easy_port }}/udp   (add clients in the UI)
  Client DNS    {{ wg_easy_dns }}
  Config dir    {{ wg_easy_dir }}

  Files         .env, compose.yml, Caddyfile (this file is chmod 600)

Common commands (run inside {{ wg_easy_dir }}):

  docker compose ps
  docker compose logs -f wg-easy
  docker compose logs -f caddy
  docker compose pull && docker compose up -d     # update images
  docker compose down                             # stop (keeps volumes)

After the first successful login the INIT_* variables in .env are no longer
needed (wg-easy ignores them once setup is done) - delete the password there to
stop keeping the plaintext on disk:

  sed -i '/^WG_ADMIN_PASSWORD=/d' .env
